{title: Come, Ye Disconsolate}
{artist: Thomas Moore & Samuel Webbe}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 69}

Verse 1
[F]Come, ye discon[Bb]solate, wher[F]e'er ye [C]languish;
[F]come to the [Dm]mercy seat, [Gm]fervently [C]kneel.
[F]Here bring your [Bb]wounded hearts, [F]here tell your [C]anguish —
[F]earth has no [Bb]sorrow that [C]heaven cannot [F]heal.

Verse 2
[F]Joy of the desolate, light [C]of
[F]the straying, Hope [Dm]of the [Gm]penitent, [C]fadeless
[F]and pure, Here [Bb]speaks [F]the Comforter, tenderly [C]saying, "Earth
[F]has no sorrow [Bb]that [C]Heav'n cannot [F]cure."

Verse 3
[F]Here see the Bread of Life; [C]see
[F]waters flowing Forth [Dm]from the throne [Gm]of [C]God,
[F]pure from above; [Bb]Come to the [F]feast of love; [C]come, ever
[F]knowing Earth has [Bb]no sorrow but [C]Heav'n can [F]remove.
